nodecode-spectator is a rewrite of Sahil-SS9's Sahil-SS9/spectator-mode:

  https://github.com/Sahil-SS9/spectator-mode
  commit a1467ded9802559b30061efe861701d8ec14bcae
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Sahil Saghir (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the whole plugin, in Common Lisp against Nodecode's own seams. The
original is a FastAPI dashboard plugin that reads the host's session database
read-only and re-serves a masked stream on a second loopback port, with its own
HMAC guest tokens, invite lifecycle, SQLite store and browser page. This cell
reads the facts the session already records in the event log instead of a host
database, serves the page on the gateway's own port through the route seam,
and keeps an invite and a suggestion in memory for the life of the process. The
mask is carried over: paths, NAME=value assignments and long opaque tokens are
rewritten before a guest reads a line. An approved suggestion enters the
session through the one in-process ingress, as the original's host injection
did.

Left out: the second HTTP server and its loopback/TLS binding rules (the
gateway's route already answers on loopback, so a tunnel supplies the remote
half), the HMAC token and its session-generation bookkeeping (a 24-character
token is the credential and dies with the process), the SQLite store and its
retention window (nothing durable is written), WebSocket streaming (the page
polls), the transcript poller with its cursor (the event log is the source),
commit-pinned branch queries over git, and the multi-harness bridge and
integrations for other CLIs, which have no meaning inside one organism. The
guest page is rewritten, smaller: the log, a suggestion box, and the poll.
